> screen, instead of centered, in the most
> space-conservative version, if not?]

If you specify its geometry as centred, it's centred.

> I don't see any need to add other extra goodies,
> though, to make it a full blown "treasure level"
> with more space than that. Sokoban is a bit of a
> "Monty-Haul" gathering rove as it is, with so many
> rings, wands, and comestibles (at least) amidst
> relatively wimpy monsters.

My test version was this:

# Tiny top level to randomise reward
MAZE:"soko0-1",' '
FLAGS:noteleport
GEOMETRY:center,center
#12345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890
MAP
 ---
--.--
|...|
-----
ENDMAP

STAIR:(02,01),down
REGION:(00,00,04,03),lit,"ordinary"
NON_DIGGABLE:(00,00,04,03)
NON_PASSWALL:(00,00,04,03)

OBJECT:'(',"bag of holding",(02,02)
TRAP:"statue",(01,02)
TRAP:"statue",(03,02)

(and likewise for soko0-2). The statue traps aren't likely to be up to
much, since it's going to be very shallow, but they add a bit of
class :-)

